# Pattern-based protection for sensitive doc types
*BLUEPRINT*.md
*ROADMAP*.md
*STRATEGY*.md
*PARTNER_APPLICATION*
*IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN*
*SMOKE_TEST*
*DEBUG_HANDOFF*
*COMPETITIVE_*
*GTM_*

# Private directories
private/
internal/
*-private/
.mcpregistry_*

# Founder reference drafts — outreach replies, 1:1 templates, private
# user notes. These contain real names and should never be committed.
data/cold-outreach/
data/users/

# Word doc exports of master-plan content. These are regeneratable from
# the .md sources and the proprietary versions live in private/master-plan/
# rather than docs/master-plan/. Belt-and-suspenders preventive.
docs/master-plan/*.docx

# GridBot runtime state & logs
scripts/gridbot/state.json
scripts/gridbot/schedule-state.json
scripts/gridbot/logs/*.jsonl

# P4.6 outreach generator — local cache for GitHub + Claude API responses.
# Per-recipient personalization (PII-adjacent) lives here; never check in.
scripts/.cache/
# P4.6 generated output — 100 emails with real names + addresses. DO NOT COMMIT.
scripts/.outreach/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Internal planning + operational docs (2026-05-14 audit cleanup)
#
# These were committed before the pattern-based protections above were added,
# then slipped into public-repo history. Phase A blocked new commits; a
# Phase B `git filter-repo` pass scrubbed the historical commits separately.
#
# To add a NEW file under one of the blanket-ignored dirs below, decide first
# whether it should be public. If yes, add an explicit `!` exception. The
# default is "internal, do not commit."
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Strategic planning at root (specific files)
/MASTER_PLAN.md
/REVENUE_MODEL_5Y.md
/DEMAND_GENERATION_PLAN.md
/NUCLEAR_EXPANSION_PLAN.md
/UNIVERSAL_EXPANSION_PLAN.md
/WEAKNESS_DEEP_RESEARCH.md
/DISCOVERY_PLAYBOOK.md
/REVIEW_MODERATION_PLAN.md
/QUALITY_MONITORING_RECOMMENDATION.md
/ONBOARDING_UX_DESIGN.md
/FRONTEND_BACKEND_AUDIT.md
/AUDIT_LOG.md
/phase-3-audit-log.md
/HANDOFF-*

# Pattern-based root protection (defense-in-depth — catches future siblings)
/*_PLAN.md
/*_MODEL*.md
/*PLAYBOOK*.md
/*_RESEARCH*.md
/*AUDIT_LOG*.md

# Internal docs directories — blanket-ignore with explicit exceptions for
# .gitkeep markers (so the directory structure persists locally)
docs/launch/
docs/master-plan/
docs/memos/
docs/plans/
docs/retrospectives/
docs/audit-failures/
!docs/audit-failures/.gitkeep
docs/phase-reports/
!docs/phase-reports/.gitkeep
docs/template-audit/
docs/content/
docs/interviews/
!docs/interviews/transcripts/.gitkeep

# docs/legal/ — internal compliance + operational SOPs by default. The
# four genuinely public-facing policy drafts are explicit exceptions.
docs/legal/
!docs/legal/aup.md
!docs/legal/acceptable-use-policy.md
!docs/legal/privacy-notice-draft.md
!docs/legal/terms-of-service-draft.md

# Internal operational data (GTM cohort details, country/waitlist state)
data/gtm/
data/international/
